# Finding A in Garnet 2.2.14 (RESULTS.md, "The three failures traced"); seed 144 of the third
# exploration. kill-now-g1 stops the primary g1 10 ms after the client's BGSAVE and keeps it down
# until the heal. Its replica g4 has received the checkpoint's markers, which g1 never committed,
# so g4's AOF tail stays above its commit point. With --aof-commit-wait every gossip reply on g4
# waits for that commit and blocks its thread for good, and g4 answers no command. The read-back
# also lacks an acknowledged RPUSH: a failover of a migration's source, finding B.
# params: device=FileStream reest=5
# commands: anytime_read first_init parallel_driver_del parallel_driver_hset parallel_driver_incr parallel_driver_lua parallel_driver_over parallel_driver_rpush parallel_driver_sadd parallel_driver_set parallel_driver_setex parallel_driver_txn parallel_driver_zadd serial_driver_failover serial_driver_migrate serial_driver_save
# expect: violation      (change to ok when the bug is fixed)
disk=none dseed=0 | run W=69274d70,p3,q1,r500,oparallel_driver_del A=garnet.bgsave+10:kill-now-g1
